The '''Volisania national football team''' represents [[Volisania]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Volisania Football Association]] and is one of the most successful teams in the [[AFA World Cup]], having won the tournament three times and remaining a regular contender in the Mesogean region.

Volisania are currently ranked 3rd in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]] and opened their [[2026 AFA World Cup|2026 World Cup]] campaign with a 3–0 win over [[Mercia national football team|Mercia]].

== History ==

=== Early success ===
Volisania were among the strongest sides of the early World Cup era, winning the tournament in 1962 and establishing themselves as a major force in Adonian football. The team developed a reputation for technical passing, possession control, and strong midfield organisation.

=== Modern era ===
The national team remained competitive through the late 20th century and added further World Cup titles in 1990 and 1998. In the modern era, Volisania have continued to qualify regularly for the tournament and remain one of the best-supported teams in the region.

== Playing style ==

Volisania are generally described as a technically refined side that emphasises controlled possession, wide attacking combinations, and structured pressing without the ball. Their squads often feature a balance of experienced domestic league players and high-profile professionals from across the Mesogean region.

